        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The outcome of elections in red states reflects broader national trends in voter behavior.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The audience understands the political context of Alabama and Southern red states.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "A candidate’s ability to win in a red state depends primarily on vote share rather than structural factors like gerrymandering or electoral college dynamics.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes it is possible to win an 'irregular' election in 2020 despite recent losses.",
