    "turn_text": "my my I am who I am and I have I've been around the block of for a long time practicing law been involved in politics for a long time studied some of these issues a lot more than others and that's just the way those numbers have worked out I don't know what those numbers are based on by the way because we so many are based on judicial nominees in which most of my, a lot of my votes have been Trump nominees for judges and for his administration. But that's just because I think the constitutional duty kind of leans that way. So I don't really know what they do that on. You know, and there's some, for instance, I don't know whether it's a Trump agenda or someone else. For instance, the banking deregulation bill, a lot of Democrats didn't vote against that, but you had 17 that did. President signed that. It was a good piece of legislation. Opioid Bill, I don't know whose agenda that was because everybody was on board with that one. It passed the Senate in 99 to 1.",
