  {
    "episode_id": 74434,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74434.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's a couple of things. Let me clarify something. And there are a number of factors. Number one, I criticized to begin with how political that decision had been made. From the very beginning, it was politicized by both Republicans and Democrats. And we are in a bad place in this country when a Supreme Court nomination is politicized the way that one started out being. It got worse as it went on, but it started out being very political. People go into their corners announcing what they were going to do. And you know, I looked at that. We spent hours and hours and hours every day for two or three months. I had a briefing on his record. It was a flawed process because we didn't get to look at all of his record. They withheld a lot. And we didn't even get to look at documents that Chairman Grassley, Chairman Judiciary had initially requested himself and the archive said he's going to take a little bit longer to do it and he went ahead with the committee hearings anyway. So number one it was a flawed process and I didn't look at that second thing I've seen documents and in there that are confidential that that for whatever reason they won't be made public for a long long time.",
