    "turn_idx": 67,
    "turn_text": "didn't make a speech about gun control. I made a speech about gun safety. And there is a difference. We've had gun regulations on the books now for 40 years. especially since 1968. But if you go back even further than that, automatic weapons have been banned in this country unless you get a special stamp and registration requirement since the days of the gangsters that used to run around with Tommy Guns. So what I think is important is that we have some common sense regulations to address gun safety. Unfortunately, we always talk about gun safety in the wake of a mass shooting in a tragedy like that. And we need to be having those dialogues more often because overwhelmingly people in this country, and I think people in the state of Alabama, who enjoy their weapons, enjoy their guns, enjoy not just hunting. They enjoy just going out and shooting in target practice, which I do. I do with my son as much as we can, which has it pin as much lately, but everyone wants to have common sense regulations that will try to keep the hands out of folks who should not have them, but allow law-abiding citizens the ability to get a firearm and enjoy it.",
