    "turn_text": "I don't see how I could at this point based on everything that's been coming out now. He has prejudged so many things. He has been, I don't think that he will protect the special counsel's investigation. If he was to come before the Senate today, I would have a very hard time to do that. However, he may be in that spot for a while, and the proof will be in his performance. And if he performs as what I think an attorney general should perform, and that is an independent voice, not the personal lawyer of the president. The attorney general is the lawyer for the people of this country, not the personal lawyer for Donald Trump or whoever is sitting in the office of the presidency. if he demonstrates that he has that independence and that he can exercise that. I don't understand about carrying out the President's agenda on criminal justice and other things. I may disagree with some of that, although the most recent one I'm all in",
