    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74434.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 108,
    "turn_text": "Well, Jeff and I have always been friends for many years. I got to know him when he was US Attorney and I was a young assistant US Attorney. We disagreed on a lot of political issues. We disagree a lot specifically on immigration and the fact that he I think went back to the days of old when trying to criminalize so many low-level drug offenders where I think you could do things differently. I think his view as Attorney General was kind of a throwback to the 70s and 80s when we were just beginning the war on drugs, which has failed miserably. So we disagree with that. But on a personal level, we've always liked each other. We've been very friendly. You know, look, I think he caught a lot of unfair criticism. He certainly did the right thing by recusing himself. He was caught in the middle of these allegations. And I believe as a lawyer, as a member of the Justice Department, he had no choice. And that's where I kind of go back that the president thought we were supposed to be loyal to him and not loyal to the department.",
