    "turn_text": "plans to do that. There is nothing like that on my radar. This book has been in the making for a long time. But my job is a lawyer. My day job is a lawyer. I was not like John Grisham who could just sit down and wait in the courtroom and just rattle off stuff. It took a lot and I got some great help. And it was just a long time coming to try to make sure that we did it the right way. And so it's just simply was time. It was an opportunity to do it and finally get it. get it in print because there are so many things about that case that I felt like. The book is not about me. It's really about how that case came together. And there are so many facts and circumstances about Birmingham and how those cases came together and the team that we had that I just felt like needed to be preserved. And I wanted to get it out two years ago, four years ago, five years ago, but it just couldn't come to fruition.",
